From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:40:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: apple: pmp: Run the PMP CPU policy on the J604 as
 well

The PMP CPU/GPU thermal policy (c4d87e269d, "thermal: apple: add the
J713 PMP CPU policy") binds only on the J713. The J604 already publishes
the same PMP telemetry: pmp-telemetry admits it and registers the
apple-pmp-thermal device, and the PMP die records read on the J604
(MEASURED on -11.3: aggregate hotspot plus Ta000m, Te000m, Te001m,
Tp000m and Tp001m in the apple_pmp hwmon). Its CPU clusters are the ones
the policy hard-codes (MEASURED: cpufreq policy0 = CPUs 0 and 7-9, P;
policy1 = CPUs 1-6, E). So nothing but the board gate keeps the policy
off the J604, which instead carried a device-tree zone with
unqualified trips.

Replace the gate by a table of qualified boards and admit the J604.
The trips, cooling envelope, 5 ms sampling and the confirmed 120 C
shutdown stay the J713's. The measured-rail power budget does not apply
to the J604: it is the J713's fanless envelope and, once the burst
energy is spent, regulates the CPU/GPU rails toward an 85 C die. The
J604's fan, which its SMC runs, is the heat path that budget stands in
for, so the J604 takes the temperature policy alone. Its rails are still
read and reported through the apple_pmp_power hwmon, and a rail read
error neither restricts the CPUs nor the GPU there.

The J604 qualification is a sustained all-core load with temperatures,
clocks and throttling recorded .

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 Documentation/soc/apple/t8132-pmp-thermal.rst |  6 +++
 drivers/thermal/Kconfig                       |  3 +-
 drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c           | 48 ++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/soc/apple/t8132-pmp-thermal.rst b/Documentation/soc/apple/t8132-pmp-thermal.rst
index e0b4872cdb..3055833746 100644
--- a/Documentation/soc/apple/t8132-pmp-thermal.rst
+++ b/Documentation/soc/apple/t8132-pmp-thermal.rst
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ temperature trips, power envelope and unmanaged CPU ceiling must not be
 described as Apple firmware limits or thermal parity with another SoC. T8132
 does not currently have a qualified effort lane in the PMP report driver.
 
+The J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4) has the same PMP records and CPU
+clusters and takes the same temperature policy. It runs without the
+measured-rail budget, which is the J713's fanless envelope: the J604's fan,
+run by its SMC, is the heat path that budget stands in for. Its rails are
+still read and reported.
+
 The historical emergency shutdown threshold is kept in
 ``pmp-emergency-policy.h`` separately from ordinary cooling tuning. This
 separation does not qualify that threshold: it remains an existing development
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/Kconfig b/drivers/thermal/Kconfig
index d7d03fa915..fa8127b961 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/thermal/Kconfig
@@ -570,7 +570,8 @@ config APPLE_PMP_THERMAL
 	help
 	  CPU/GPU cooling, measured-rail power budgets and fault guards fed by the PMP
 	  firmware owner. Higher CPU states remain capped until protection is
-	  installed. The sensor topology is qualified for J713 only. Cooling,
+	  installed. The sensor topology is qualified for J713 and J604; the
+	  J604, which has a fan, runs without the rail budget. Cooling,
 	  measured-rail budgets and the separate emergency shutdown are provisional
 	  Linux policies, not Apple firmware limits. A T8132 firmware effort lane,
 	  emergency limit and advancing telemetry heartbeat remain unqualified.
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c b/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
index 203ea9f560..46dc59af88 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only OR MIT
 /*
- * J713 CPU/GPU thermal policy using read-only samples from the PMP owner.
+ * T8132 (J713, J604) CPU/GPU thermal policy using read-only samples from the
+ * PMP owner.
  * The policy and thresholds are carried from the existing M4 implementation;
  * these are Linux operating limits, not inferred Apple hardware safety limits.
  * Guards are installed before cpufreq relinquishes its unmanaged ceiling.
@@ -40,6 +41,25 @@
 #define APPLE_PMP_POLL_MS		5
 #define APPLE_PMP_GOVERNOR_NS	100000000ULL
 
+/*
+ * Boards whose sensor topology and operating policy are qualified: the PMP
+ * die records, P cores 0 and 7-9, E cores 1-6. The measured-rail budget is
+ * the J713's fanless envelope (it regulates toward 85 C once the burst
+ * energy is spent). The J604 has a fan that its SMC runs, so it takes the
+ * temperature policy alone: the same trips, cooling envelope and shutdown
+ * backstop, without the rail budget. Its rails are still read and reported.
+ */
+struct apple_pmp_board {
+	const char *compatible;
+	const char *name;
+	bool rail_budget;
+};
+
+static const struct apple_pmp_board apple_pmp_boards[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j713", .name = "J713", .rail_budget = true },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j604", .name = "J604", .rail_budget = false },
+};
+
 struct apple_pmp_cluster {
 	struct cpufreq_policy *policy;
 	struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev;
@@ -47,6 +67,7 @@ struct apple_pmp_cluster {
 };
 
 static struct {
+	const struct apple_pmp_board *board;
 	const struct apple_pmp_sensor_data *sensors;
 	struct thermal_zone_device *zone;
 	struct apple_pmp_cluster clusters[2];
@@ -199,14 +220,15 @@ static void apple_pmp_power_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		active |= BIT(2);
 	apple_pmp_power_set_active(p, active);
 	apple_pmp_power_sample(p, now, mw, pmp_thermal.cached_mc, ret);
-	apple_pmp_gpu_publish(pmp_thermal.sensors, epoch, p->level[2],
+	apple_pmp_gpu_publish(pmp_thermal.sensors, epoch,
+			      pmp_thermal.board->rail_budget ? p->level[2] : 0,
 			      active & BIT(2) ? p->last_ns : 0);
 	pr_debug("apple-pmp-thermal: power ns=%llu mc=%ld p_mw=%u e_mw=%u gpu_mw=%u total_mw=%d sustainable_mw=%d allowed_mw=%d credit_mj=%lld p_level=%u e_level=%u gpu_level=%u error=%d\n",
 		now, pmp_thermal.cached_mc, mw[0], mw[1], mw[2], p->total_mw,
 		p->sustainable_mw, p->allowed_mw, p->credit_mj,
 		p->level[0], p->level[1], p->level[2], ret);
 	mutex_unlock(&pmp_thermal.lock);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret && pmp_thermal.board->rail_budget)
 		pr_warn_ratelimited("apple-pmp-thermal: power telemetry error %d, retaining minimum CPU/GPU ceilings\n",
 				    ret);
 	schedule_delayed_work(&pmp_thermal.power_work, msecs_to_jiffies(500));
@@ -329,7 +351,9 @@ static int apple_pmp_guard(unsigned int level)
 		unsigned int power_level = pmp_thermal.power.level[i];
 		unsigned int effective;
 
-		if (!pmp_thermal.power.last_ns || ktime_get_ns() -
+		if (!pmp_thermal.board->rail_budget)
+			power_level = 0;
+		else if (!pmp_thermal.power.last_ns || ktime_get_ns() -
 		    pmp_thermal.power.last_ns > APPLE_PMP_POWER_STALE_NS)
 			power_level = 8;
 		effective = max(level, power_level);
@@ -713,7 +737,9 @@ static int apple_pmp_thermal_setup(void)
 		if (ret)
 			goto fail;
 	}
-	pr_info("apple-pmp-thermal: J713 provisional policy: CPU/GPU cooling from 106 C, target 110 C, full protection 115 C, three >=120 C samples for shutdown, 5 ms sampling/100 ms governor, shared measured-rail power budget\n");
+	pr_info("apple-pmp-thermal: %s provisional policy: CPU/GPU cooling from 106 C, target 110 C, full protection 115 C, three >=120 C samples for shutdown, 5 ms sampling/100 ms governor, %s\n",
+		pmp_thermal.board->name, pmp_thermal.board->rail_budget ?
+		"shared measured-rail power budget" : "no rail budget (fan under SMC control)");
 	pmp_thermal.ready = true;
 	return 0;
 fail:
@@ -738,12 +764,20 @@ static void apple_pmp_thermal_setup_work(struct work_struct *work)
 static int apple_pmp_thermal_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	const struct apple_pmp_sensor_data *sensors = dev_get_platdata(&pdev->dev);
+	const struct apple_pmp_board *board = NULL;
+	unsigned int i;
 
-	/* Only this board's sensor topology and operating policy are qualified. */
-	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713"))
+	/* Only these boards' sensor topology and operating policy are qualified. */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(apple_pmp_boards); i++)
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible(apple_pmp_boards[i].compatible)) {
+			board = &apple_pmp_boards[i];
+			break;
+		}
+	if (!board)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	if (!sensors || !sensors->read || !sensors->dev)
 		return -EINVAL;
+	pmp_thermal.board = board;
 	pmp_thermal.sensors = sensors;
 	pmp_thermal.cached_error = -EAGAIN;
 	pmp_thermal.power_error = -EAGAIN;
